When a job card’s “History” section is expanded, it currently grows the entire grid row, stretching sibling cards to match its height — this is CSS Grid’s default row-sizing behavior and needs to be fixed at the root, not just visually patched.
Desired behavior: clicking “History” should make that card visually pop to the front — elevate it above the grid (higher z-index, a subtle scale-up, and a stronger shadow) — and take it out of normal grid document flow while expanded (e.g., position it absolutely/fixed over its original spot, or render it as an overlay), so sibling cards in the same row stay completely unaffected at their original size. Use Framer Motion for the animation (add it as a new dependency) so the “pop forward” and the height expansion both animate smoothly together, not as two separate abrupt steps.
Cap the expanded history list with a max-height and make it internally scrollable once entries exceed that height — reuse the exact same thin, pill-shaped, auto-hiding scrollbar already used in the log console viewer. Extract that scrollbar styling into one shared reusable class if it isn’t already, and apply it consistently to every scrollable area in the app, not just this one.
Clicking anywhere outside the expanded card should collapse it back to its original size and position in the grid, with the same animation reversed.
